  },
  {
    key: 'compliance-computability',
    brief: `Scope: task rules and computability. From ${REPO} (read-only): git log --oneline 15d099d..HEAD (one French commit per step, in order 1-6); git diff --stat 15d099d HEAD (only formal/); run '${LAKE} build' from ${REPO}/formal and count warnings; run the forbidden-token grep from AGENTS.md; generate a scratch file with '#print axioms' for EVERY theorem and EVERY def of the module (including Ern.MM02.Witness.*) and check: theorems within {propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice}; operations and checked variants (read, write, dealloc, alloc, checkedRead, checkedWrite, checkedDealloc, readBytes) without Classical.choice; grep the module for 'noncomputable', 'Classical', 'propDecidable', 'Decidable.decide' hacks or 'implemented_by'. Check every required name exists with the required type (readBytes : State → Access → Option (List AByte); Outcome' (α : Type) with ok (s : State) (v : α) | fail (s : State) | ub; checkedRead returning Outcome' (List AByte); Aligned, Inv, State.empty, inv_empty, Reachable, reachable_inv, write_absent, dealloc_absent, AllocPreDec, required instances). Check every def/theorem/instance/structure/inductive has a docstring citing an MM rule. Check step 6: for EACH raw and checked operation one ok witness and one ub (resp. fail) witness, on states built from State.empty, ObR/ObW trivial, Compatible equality, checked by decide or #eval on a Bool projection, never on the state; #eval witnesses of the value read after write for readBytes and checkedRead. Check nothing out of scope (carve/revoke/merge, MM-03, F, G). Report only violations.`,
