Check that each relation says exactly what the brief step 1 and the arbitrations say, not stronger, not weaker: ok with the existing effect iff kernel precondition ∧ dec ∧ stat (resp. CanDealloc, AllocPre unbounded form); ub otherwise; total on all states; no Inv/WF in constructors; no Decidable required by the definitions. Check that every theorem statement has the exact shape the brief requires (e.g. read_complete : ReadStep … o → ∀ hs, read … hs = o; alloc agreement under WF only). Check that ReachableStep matches step 4 and that the equivalence with Reachable is stated as an equivalence. Check MM-02.H, MM-01.5, MM-02.B/C/D/2 quotes for any mismatch (e.g. does the ok outcome of the read relation need a value per MM-02.H?). Check that hypotheses are satisfiable (no vacuous theorem) and that definitions are not too permissive. Read definitions, hypotheses and quantifiers, not only proofs.` },
  { key: 'lean', prompt: `Lens: LEAN RIGOR AND RULE COMPLIANCE.
