input.script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'review-mm02-p4',
  description: 'Adversarial review of MM-02 v0.3 pass 4: 4 lens finders, each verified by a refuting judge',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Find', detail: 'four lenses over module and report' },
    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'one refuting judge per finder batch' },
  ],
}

const SP = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad'
const CONTEXT = `
Context (read the files; do not rely on this summary for semantics):
- Repo: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern, branch formal/memory_model_0.3. Pass-4 commits sit on top of 1c1b90e (end of pass 3): 916df80, 4a65d81, f93bdff, fb85d5a, 3668375, 25ee0aa.
- Task brief for this pass (authoritative, includes "Arbitrages"): ${SP}/task03p4.md. Pass-3 brief: ${SP}/task03p3.md.
- Spec (normative, outside the repo): /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_Memory_Model_v0.3_consolidee.md
- Module: formal/Ern/MM02.lean (namespace Ern.MM02). Pass-3 version: ${SP}/mm02_p3.lean (= git show 1c1b90e:formal/Ern/MM02.lean).
- Report under review (uncommitted): formal/reports/MM02_v0.3_p4.md. Pass-3 report: formal/reports/MM02_v0.3_p3.md.
- formal/DESIGN.md and AGENTS.md (review rules: evidence required for every finding; never ask for additions beyond the task).
- Lean: lake is at ~/.elan/bin/lake. The module is already built. Do NOT run \`lake build\` and do NOT modify any file in the repo (no edits, no git checkout/commit/stash). To test something, write a scratch .lean file under ${SP}/ named p4rev_<something>.lean, starting with \`import Ern\` and \`open Ern.MM02\` (add \`import Lean\` first for meta code), and run: cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <file>.
- Existing evidence: axiom sweep over all 154 named declarations ${SP}/axall_p4.txt; decision-instance reachability check ${SP}/p4_nodec.lean; per-declaration statement diff p3→p4 ${SP}/p4_diffdecls.txt; section (i) evidence ${SP}/p4_i_evidence.lean; old-vs-new reachability coverage ${SP}/p4_reach_cover.lean.
`

const FINDINGS = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    findings: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          id: { type: 'string' },
          title: { type: 'string' },
          location: { type: 'string' },
          claim: { type: 'string' },
          evidence: { type: 'string' },
          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocking', 'major', 'minor'] },
          cause: { type: 'string', enum: ['formalization', 'coverage', 'report', 'spec', 'brief'] },
          fix: { type: 'string' },
        },
        required: ['id', 'title', 'location', 'claim', 'evidence', 'severity', 'cause', 'fix'],
      },
    },
  },
  required: ['findings'],
}

const VERDICTS = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    verdicts: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          id: { type: 'string' },
          status: { type: 'string', enum: ['confirmed', 'refuted', 'unverified'] },
          evidence: { type: 'string' },
          fix: { type: 'string' },
        },
        required: ['id', 'status', 'evidence', 'fix'],
      },
    },
  },
  required: ['verdicts'],
}

const FINDERS = [
  { key: 'spec', prompt: `Lens: SPEC AND BRIEF FIDELITY. For each of the 5 steps of the pass-4 brief and each arbitration, check the module does exactly what is asked, not more, not less: ReadOblSpec/WriteOblSpec without instance, ReadObl/WriteObl extending them with decInst and projection toSpec; ReadStep/WriteStep on the *Spec, interpreters on ReadObl/WriteObl; ReadOutcome; ReadStep_ok_iff fixing v = Alloc.bytesAt …; the four read agreement theorems with EXACTLY the brief's statements; read unchanged; no Outcome ↔ ReadOutcome conversion; alloc taking (hwf : WF s); alloc_sound/alloc_complete with no other hypothesis; alloc_eq_ok on AllocPre; alloc_eq_ok_of_wf removed; Reachable Compatible ObR ObW s and ReachableStep Compatible ObR.toSpec ObW.toSpec s with the same parameters on both sides; full-relation replacement removed. Check the arbitration "Ne pas masquer cette asymétrie par un théorème de complétude plus général que son domaine" against every completeness theorem. Check "aucune précondition normative assouplie, aucun énoncé affaibli": compare every rewritten statement with its pass-3 form (${SP}/p4_diffdecls.txt) and look for a real weakening.` },
  { key: 'lean', prompt: `Lens: LEAN RIGOR. Verify with commands: AGENTS.md forbidden-term grep from the repo root; #print axioms on every new or rewritten declaration (Classical.choice allowed ONLY in the four *_total theorems); every new def/inductive/structure/theorem cites a spec location in its docstring; no noncomputable. Check the claim "Les relations ne dépendent d'aucune instance de décision" with your own meta check (do not trust p4_nodec.lean blindly): which decision instances do ReadStep, WriteStep, DeallocStep, AllocStep, ReachableStep reach, and through what. Try mutation tests in scratch files: e.g. would every theorem still hold if ReadStep.ok returned a different value, or if the Reachable alloc constructor dropped hwf? Report a property the theorem set fails to pin down only if the brief asked for it.` },
  { key: 'report', prompt: `Lens: REPORT ACCURACY. Check every factual claim in formal/reports/MM02_v0.3_p4.md against the module and command output: counts (91 theorems, 5 removed, 6 added, 16 rewritten theorems, 154 named declarations, 4 examples and 2 witness definitions), the axiom lists in (g), the claims in (i) (re-run ${SP}/p4_i_evidence.lean), and above all section (j): it must be an EXHAUSTIVE list of statements rewritten in this pass with old and new forms side by side. Independently diff 1c1b90e..HEAD on formal/Ern/MM02.lean and look for any rewritten statement or definition missing from (j), or listed wrongly (wrong old/new form). Check the "Docstrings modifiées" list. Check verbatim quotations from the spec and DESIGN.md (DESIGN.md has markdown bold around "Semantics"). Check cross-references to pass-2/pass-3 report sections. Check that sections (a)-(g), (i), (j) exist.` },
  { key: 'arbitration', prompt: `Lens: ARBITRATION, SCOPE AND COMPLETENESS. (1) Out of scope must stay out (defined reservation failure, MM-03, MVS, carve/revoke/merge, data stacks, F, G, dec/stat split). (2) No interpretation silently chosen where the spec or brief is unclear; check the report's (c) and (e) list every such choice (e.g. how "leurs prédicats peuvent dépendre de l'état et de l'opération" applies to Compatible; whether decision instances inside the effects violate "Les relations ne dépendent d'aucune instance de décision"; the extra hwf argument on Reachable.alloc; ReachableStep.read being a no-op step). (3) Section (i): is the list of relation outcomes the interpreters cannot produce complete and correct? Look for missed or wrong cases. (4) Section (f): DESIGN.md tensions complete and correctly stated, in particular the claim that the interpreter-agreement tension is lifted. (5) Section (j) justifications: is the "not weakened" argument for reachable_inv/reachableStep_inv sound (re-run ${SP}/p4_reach_cover.lean)?` },
]

const results = await pipeline(
  FINDERS,
  f => agent(`You are an adversarial, read-only reviewer of a Lean 4 formalization pass.\n${CONTEXT}\n${f.prompt}\n\nReturn only findings you can back with evidence (spec/brief quote, counterexample, or command output you actually ran). Do not request additions beyond the task. Return an empty list if nothing survives your own scrutiny.`,
    { label: `find:${f.key}`, phase: 'Find', schema: FINDINGS }),
  (r, f) => {
    const fs = (r && r.findings) || []
    if (!fs.length) return { key: f.key, findings: [], verdicts: [] }
    return agent(`You are a skeptical judge. Your job is to REFUTE each finding below if you can; default to "refuted" when the evidence does not hold up, and "unverified" only if you could not check it. Re-run every command or Lean snippet the finding relies on; read the cited spec/brief text yourself.\n${CONTEXT}\nA finding is confirmed only if (a) its evidence holds when you re-check it and (b) it is within the task scope of the brief (findings that ask for additions beyond the brief are refuted). For each confirmed finding give the smallest correct fix.\n\nFindings (lens: ${f.key}):\n${JSON.stringify(fs, null, 2)}`,
      { label: `verify:${f.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICTS })
      .then(v => ({ key: f.key, findings: fs, verdicts: (v && v.verdicts) || [] }))
  },
)

return results.filter(Boolean)

